#N canvas 0 50 1040 1300 12;
#X text 30 16 =^..^=   tx81z~   version 1 (2026)   sofia vallejo budziszewski   iem kug graz austria;
#X text 30 46 tx81z style 4-operator fm synth;
#X text 30 86 four sine-based operators with eight waveforms each and eight algorithms. every operator has a frequency ratio a fine tune and its own adsr. operator 4 has feedback. lfo to pitch and amplitude. eight voices., f 110;
#X text 30 146 --- how it was made ---;
#X text 30 190 each operator is a phase-modulated oscillator. the output of a modulator is added to the phase of the next operator so the algorithm decides who modulates whom., f 110;
#X text 30 240 the eight waveforms are sine and seven shapes cut from it (half rectified full rectified quarter pulses double speed and square types)., f 110;
#X text 30 290 operator 4 feeds back into itself for a rougher spectrum. envelopes are adsr per operator., f 110;
#X text 30 330 --- how to use ---;
#X text 30 374 1  open the engine page below and turn dsp on, f 110;
#X text 30 404 2  play a midi keyboard or click chord on, f 110;
#X text 30 434 3  open the parameters page and move any control or open presets and step through the sounds, f 110;
#X text 30 464 4  everything is a message: see the messages page for the full list and the examples page for patches to copy, f 110;
#X text 30 524 try:  switch wave2 to half sine and raise level2: the modulator gets brighter without a new operator, f 110;
#X text 30 554 try:  raise feedback on algorithm 1: operator 4 turns from sine to saw-like and the whole chain brightens, f 110;
#X text 30 604 try:  pick algorithm 8 and set all ratios to harmonics: you have an additive organ, f 110;
#X text 30 648 --- common problems ---;
#X text 30 692 no sound: turn dsp on in the engine page and check the volume slider. the synth needs a note: click chord on or play a midi key, f 110;
#X text 30 742 nothing changes after a rebuild: pd keeps the old external in memory so close every patch and restart pd, f 110;
#X text 30 772 a note is stuck: send panic. a missing note off from a midi device is the usual cause, f 110;
#X text 30 802 unknown parameter in the console: names are exact and lowercase so send params to print them all, f 110;
#X text 30 832 a bank file is not found: save and load names are relative to the folder of this patch, f 110;
#X text 30 862 the sliders do not move when you change a preset: the object must be created with the same name as in the boxes. default name is the object name, f 110;
#X text 30 912 clicks or dropouts: raise the audio buffer in the pd audio settings or lower the voice count in the creation argument, f 110;
#X text 30 962 no sound from an operator: operators 2 to 4 are modulators in most algorithms so listen for them in algorithm 8, f 110;
#X text 30 1012 harsh and noisy: lower level on the modulators or lower feedback, f 110;
#X text 30 1056 --- click a box to open that page ---;
#N canvas 0 50 900 1076 presets 0;
#X text 30 16 presets: factory sounds are stored as plain text and every control above is a message. click a box to load that sound, f 100;
#X text 30 66 --- factory presets ---;
#X msg 30 110 \; tx81z preset 0;
#X text 250 112 0  soft keys;
#X msg 30 144 \; tx81z preset 1;
